\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The real geography is quite useful. A ground-truthed description puts 
\f1\b Willoughby Road to West Street at about 400 m
\f0\b0 , much of it a straight bushland section; the Sublime Point reserve lies immediately west of Sublime Point Road between Willoughby and the backs of the West Street properties. Sublime Point Road is a sealed dead-end road, and the real lookout lies farther south. With your Shakti gate 
\f1\b 100 m north of West Street
\f0\b0 , you have only about 
\f1\b 300 m between the first Willoughby roadblock and the compound gate
\f0\b0 . That is a very compressed military corridor. ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://naturetrail.com.au/blog-post/missing-gary-tweddle-book-part-19-chapter-6-our-own-ground-truthing/?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 Nature Trail}})\
