\f2 \cf0 <$Scr_H::3>
\f1\b\fs28 4. The Fridge Force trigger\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f0 I think the clean solution is:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Fridge Force does not choose UDF over the Elvi on moral or investigative grounds. The UDF becomes the first active obstruction to Fridge Force's recovery operation.
\f0\b0 \
Fridge Force knows the Elvi stole the Gyges discs. The manuscript already establishes that as their institutional reason for being there: stolen regulated stasis components have ended up in unauthorised experimentation at Sublime Point/Ruined Castle.\
But the purpose of the MoSES operation is 
\f1\b recover/control the discs and shut down the dangerous field activity
\f0\b0 , not punish whoever committed the original burglary.\
So the sequence can be:\

\f1\b MoSES arrives and performs the spectacular drone show.
\f0\b0 \
While everybody watches, an element goes towards the lookout/Ruined Castle access (the only access is via underground access through Sublime Point).\
The UDF detects that movement. Its counter-drone system tracks or jams it. An officer orders the unknown drones out of the military exclusion zone.\
The UDF commander, like any UDF officer, had been trained to consider Fridge Force to be terrifying (that\'92s part of the gag).\

\f1\b The UDF fires first\'97or at minimum obtains weapons lock and attempts electronic suppression.
\f0\b0 \
At that instant the UDF becomes the immediate hazard to the recovery operation.\
Then the pentad drone groups stop being entertainment.\

\f1\b The Elvi are known thieves.\uc0\u8232 The UDF are the people currently shooting at Fridge Force.
\f0\b0 \
Fridge Force can deal with evidence and thieves afterwards.\
Then, once the Elvi activate or start 
\f1\b throwing stolen Gyges discs
\f0\b0 , they move instantly from 
\f4\i persons associated with stolen property
\f0\i0  to 
\f4\i persons actively deploying regulated stasis components in a combat zone
\f0\i0 . MoSES starts forming around them too.\
That is much more Fridge Force: no allegiance to Dunhilton, Eloise or the Elvi; just an organisation enforcing its own technical jurisdiction with terrifying competence.\
}